---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { REPO, REQUEST_URL } from "../data/catalogue";

// Each donation link shows only once its account exists. Turn one on with live: true, and list it
// in .github/FUNDING.yml ("github: sapience-design", "ko_fi: freethetools") so the repository's
// Sponsor button offers it too. The section hides while no link is live.
const GIVE = [
  { live: false, href: "https://github.com/sponsors/sapience-design", label: "Sponsor on GitHub", icon: "heart" },
  { live: true, href: "https://ko-fi.com/freethetools", label: "One-off on Ko-fi", icon: "coffee" },
].filter((g) => g.live);
const DONATIONS = GIVE.length > 0;
const description = DONATIONS
  ? "Free the Tools stays free, with no ads and no paid version. If it saved you time, you can buy the maintainers a coffee, build a tool, or tell someone about it."
  : "Free the Tools stays free, with no ads and no paid version. If it saved you time, you can build a tool, ask for one, or tell someone about it.";
---
<Base
  page="support"
  title="Support Free the Tools"
  description={description}
  jsonLd={{ "@type": "WebPage", name: "Support Free the Tools", url: "https://freethetools.com/support/" }}
>
  <div class="page narrow support">
    <a class="back" href="/"><Icon name="caret-left" />All tools</a>
    <div class="intro">
      <h1 class="h1">Support Free the Tools</h1>
      <p class="lede">Every tool is free, with no limits, no ads and no paid version. That will not change. If the tools saved you time, here is how to give something back.</p>
    </div>

    {DONATIONS && (<section aria-labelledby="coffee-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="coffee-h">Buy the maintainers a coffee</h2>
      <p>Donations pay for the domain and the time it takes to review tools and keep the site safe. Nothing is unlocked by paying, and nothing is taken away by not paying.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        {GIVE.map((g, i) => <a class={i === 0 ? "btn" : "btn line"} href={g.href} rel="noopener">{g.icon && <Icon name={g.icon} />}{g.label}</a>)}
      </div>
      <p class="muted">{GIVE.length > 1 ? "Both are plain links" : "It is a plain link"} to {GIVE.length > 1 ? "those sites" : "that site"}. This page loads nothing from {GIVE.length > 1 ? "them" : "it"} and sends {GIVE.length > 1 ? "them" : "it"} nothing about you.</p>
    </section>)}

    <section aria-labelledby="build-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="build-h">Build or request a tool</h2>
      <p>Most tools take an afternoon, and the <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>contributor guide</a> walks you through it. Your name goes on the tool page. If you cannot build it, <a href={REQUEST_URL}>ask for it</a> and others can vote.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="spread-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="spread-h">Tell someone</h2>
      <p>The site has no ads and no tracking, so it grows only when people pass it on. Send a tool to someone who still uploads their documents to a stranger's server, or <a href={`${REPO}`}>star the project on GitHub</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="company-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="company-h">For companies: sponsor a tool</h2>
      <p>A company can fund the build of a tool people have asked for. The tool page then credits the company by name. That is all a sponsor gets: no placement, no ranking, no data, no say over the pledge. Sapience AS invoices sponsorship with Norwegian VAT. Write to <a href="mailto:hello@freethetools.com">hello@freethetools.com</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="where-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="where-h">Where the money goes</h2>
      <p>Hosting is free on Cloudflare. The costs are the domain, the time to review contributions, security work and the occasional library licence check. Any surplus goes into building the tools people have asked for most. The <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/GOVERNANCE.md`}>governance page</a> sets the rules, including that sponsorship can never buy features or tracking.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .support { display: grid; gap: 28px; }
  .intro { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  section { display: grid; gap: 10px; padding-top: 8px; }
  section p { color: var(--soft); margin: 0; }
  section a:not(.btn) { color: var(--ink); }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }
  .muted { font-size: 0.9em; }
</style>
